I will attempt the `edit_file` one last time with the exact line content.Let me re-read the exact lines around line 86 to get the precise whitespace.Let me see the entire file so I can use `write_file` instead.Here's the bug:

**Line 86**: `handlers.splice(handlers.indexOf(handler), 1);`

When `handler` is not in the array, `indexOf` returns `-1`. Calling `splice(-1, 1)` removes the **last** element of the array (not index `-1` — negative indices count from the end in JS/TS). This silently removes a different handler without any error.

The fix is to only splice when the handler was actually found:The edit succeeded. Let me verify the fix is correct and run the project's check command.Let me run the typecheck and verify there are no test failures.**Bug cause:** On line 86, `handlers.splice(handlers.indexOf(handler), 1)` was called without checking whether `handler` actually existed in the array. When `indexOf()` returns `-1` (not found), `splice(-1, 1)` removes the **last** element of the array instead of doing nothing — silently deleting a different handler.

**Fix:** Store the result of `indexOf(handler)`, and only call `splice()` if the result is not `-1`. This makes `off(type, handler)` a no-op when the handler wasn't registered for that type, rather than silently corrupting the handlers list.

